From d36f23819158458e61e03692cb5f3ece714c49df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 22:53:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(tools): .camtools carries the tool body; "Import tool
 holders" toggle

A tool library entry's definition may carry `body`, the ToolBodyDto a
.camproj tool stores (drawn holder profile, placed mesh, lathe holder).
Additive: old files read unchanged and older builds ignore the key.
Export writes it; the reader judges it as the project loader does
(re-derived envelope, fitted to its tool) and refuses the file naming
the tool otherwise.

The import takes the holders choice as a parameter of the one undoable
ImportTools command (with_holders); the Tool library page gets an
"Import tool holders" checkbox (default on, remembered per user in the
prefs file) and MCP import_tool_library an optional `holders` flag.
Off lands every tool bare. The identical-tool skip compares the body
only when one lands. camcraft-mcp skill doc updated; PROCESS_VERSION 17.

Fixes #889

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX
